{"availability":"available","full":"ethangreeney/atlas","name":"atlas","description":"Every country, capital, flag and map, learned with FSRS spaced repetition. Free, keyboard-first, works offline.","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-22T03:53:02Z","updated":"2026-10-11T01:36:46Z","branch":"master","homepage":"https://atlasgeo.pages.dev","topics":["fsrs","geography","pwa","spaced-repetition"],"demo":"https://atlasgeo.pages.dev/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.043Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.043Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.043Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.043Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Every country, capital, flag and map, learned with spaced repetition. Free, no account needed.","I play Krillion and GeoGuessr and kept losing on the same things: micro-states in the Pacific and Caribbean, capitals nobody mentions, flags that look alike. The best material for this is the Ultimate Geography Anki deck, but the Anki apps are dated and fiddly. Atlas is that deck with a front end I actually want to open every day: it starts straight into today's cards, everything is a keystroke, and the scheduler is FSRS, the same algorithm Anki uses, tuned to the settings its authors recommend."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ethangreeney/atlas/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"63c5b00a5f78b5051983f5cc55de2d413ec1631f89c28864eecca93229de2c18","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.176Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:09.176Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Every country, capital, flag and map, learned with spaced repetition. Free, no account needed.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/ethangreeney/atlas/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"Free, no account needed.","sourceUrl":"https://gith